@page "/"
@layout MarketingLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Needly · The Action Inbox for GitHub</PageTitle>

<main class="marketing-home">
	<section class="marketing-hero" aria-labelledby="marketing-title">
		<div class="marketing-hero-copy">
			<p class="marketing-kicker">GitHub App powered action inbox</p>
			<h1 id="marketing-title">Needly turns GitHub noise into a queue your team can finish.</h1>
			<p class="marketing-lede">
				Review requests, failed checks, unresolved feedback, mentions, and merge-ready pull requests become clear actions with ownership, risk, and next steps.
			</p>
			<div class="marketing-hero-actions">
				<MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/auth/login" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Login">
					Connect GitHub
				</MudButton>
				<MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/inbox" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Inbox">
					View inbox
				</MudButton>
			</div>
			<dl class="marketing-proof-strip" aria-label="Needly product proof points">
				<div>
					<dt>Signed</dt>
					<dd>Webhook verification</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Durable</dt>
					<dd>Event persistence</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Team-aware</dt>
					<dd>Direct and team assignments</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</div>

		<div class="marketing-console" aria-label="Needly inbox preview">
			<div class="console-topbar">
				<span></span>
				<span></span>
				<span></span>
				<strong>Action Inbox</strong>
			</div>
			<div class="console-summary">
				<span>Today</span>
				<strong>12 actions need a decision</strong>
			</div>
			<div class="console-row console-row-critical">
				<span class="console-pill">Fix</span>
				<div>
					<strong>CI failed on checkout hardening</strong>
					<small>kasuken/Needly · waiting 36m · owner: platform</small>
				</div>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.WarningAmber"/>
			</div>
			<div class="console-row">
				<span class="console-pill">Review</span>
				<div>
					<strong>PR ready for architecture review</strong>
					<small>team request · at risk in 4h</small>
				</div>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.RateReview"/>
			</div>
			<div class="console-row">
				<span class="console-pill">Merge</span>
				<div>
					<strong>All checks passed, approvals met</strong>
					<small>release workflow · no blockers</small>
				</div>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Merge"/>
			</div>
			<div class="console-footer">
				<span>Rules applied</span>
				<strong>Pin critical, snooze FYI, archive closed</strong>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="how-it-works" class="marketing-band marketing-flow" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
		<div>
			<p class="marketing-kicker">Workflow</p>
			<h2 id="flow-title">From webhook to decision, without the notification fog.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="flow-grid">
			<article>
				<span>01</span>
				<h3>Receive</h3>
				<p>GitHub App webhooks are verified, persisted, deduplicated, and processed after acknowledgement.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<span>02</span>
				<h3>Detect</h3>
				<p>Needly recognizes review requests, unresolved comments, failed checks, mentions, stale work, and merge readiness.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<span>03</span>
				<h3>Focus</h3>
				<p>Saved views, team visibility, and automation rules shape the work into a practical queue.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="features" class="marketing-band feature-matrix" aria-labelledby="features-title">
		<div class="section-heading">
			<p class="marketing-kicker">Built for maintainers</p>
			<h2 id="features-title">A focused operating surface for GitHub teams.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="feature-grid">
			<article>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.FilterAlt"/>
				<h3>Saved Views</h3>
				<p>Reusable filters for action type, state, repository, organization, author, assignee scope, wait time, and bot involvement.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Rule"/>
				<h3>Automation Rules</h3>
				<p>Automatically pin, archive, mute, snooze, or mark matching actions as FYI.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Groups"/>
				<h3>Team Visibility</h3>
				<p>Separate direct assignments from team requests so shared ownership stays visible.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.History"/>
				<h3>Resumable Bootstrap</h3>
				<p>Import existing open work after installation while new webhooks keep flowing through the same durable pipeline.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="teams" class="marketing-band marketing-split" aria-labelledby="teams-title">
		<div>
			<p class="marketing-kicker">Why it matters</p>
			<h2 id="teams-title">GitHub records activity. Needly asks what action survives it.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="split-copy">
			<p>
				Teams do not need another stream. They need a place where work can be triaged, delegated, snoozed, muted, reopened, and eventually finished.
			</p>
			<a class="marketing-text-link" href="https://github.com/kasuken/Needly" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the repository</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</main>